## Operator notes (when present)

The human may have added notes that override or refine the investigator's recommendation. Treat them with priority:

- "Apply as proposed" / "Looks good" / similar → proceed with the proposed_action gate below.
- "Don't apply X" / "Skip the rename" / "False positive" → call `kg_finding_resolve(finding_id, action="no_action", reason="<quote operator note>", notes="<note text>")` and return_control. Do not call the mutation tool.
- "Apply but with Y instead of X" / a refined arg → if the change is minor (e.g. different label spelling, different keep_id within the same pair), apply with the operator's value; quote the operator note in the mutation tool's `reason`. If the change is large enough to be a different action than proposed_action.op, escalate.
- Anything ambiguous → escalate via `kg_finding_escalate` with the operator's note in the summary.

Quote the operator note verbatim in the mutation tool's `reason` (or in `kg_finding_resolve.reason`) so the kg_revision_log shows whose call this was.

